  "note": "The D435i (with its 6-DoF IMU, BMI085 by the product code table; not modelled) with an IR-pass filter on the cover glass. The IR-pass filter: \"CLAREX NIR-75N near-infrared filter applied to cover glass, with holes over projector and RGB sensor openings. Filter transmits near-infrared light and absorbs visible light. Filter's thickness = 0.5 mm\" (Table 2-2 notes); Table 3-50 compares the f line: false depth from repetitive patterns and saturation from specular reflections mitigated, indoor range \"limited by IR projector power\", left/right images limited by ambient IR. Poses: the body origin is the left imager's optical centre, the datasheet's depth origin (section 4.8.1); the right imager one baseline along -y, optical axes parallel to body x (the rectified geometry). The projector is placed at the baseline midpoint as an ASSUMPTION (pose_stated false; drawn but not dimensioned). Not stated: pixel size, distortion coefficients (\"Distortion <= 1.5%\"), subpixel accuracy: the lens model is pinhole, a labelled assumption. FOVs vary by about +/-3 degrees unit to unit (Table 3-49 note 3). max_range_m is the upper figure of the \"Range\" feature line (\"over\", \"varies with lighting conditions\"). Streams are the USB 3.1 Gen 1 tables; power_w is the \"All Components\" power at the Max Operating Mode (section 7.4). The RGB camera (OV2740, rolling shutter per the store page, 69 x 42 degrees) is \"not integrated in the module\" and its offset is not stated: placed at the depth origin as an ASSUMPTION (pose_stated false). Depth start point 4.7 mm behind the front glass (Table 4-17). size_mm: 90 x 25.8 x 25 mm (store page; Table 3-52 note: depth \"around 25.8mm\"). Mass 75 g (Table 3-52). Only the depth sensor takes the external trigger (section 3.7.4). Store page: ideal range 0.3-3 m, min-Z ~28 cm, accuracy <2% at 2 m.",
